      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6197204::web::019::microhardness_and_magnetic_properties"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The ordered regions and precipitates will be dispersed within an fcc matrix.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11426066::web::019::conclusion"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Rapid quenching will freeze in the partially ordered microstructure created during annealing.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Partial ordering and nanoscale precipitates will create local magnetic anisotropy.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11426066::web::019::conclusion"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The resulting microstructural features will strengthen domain-wall pinning.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11426066::web::019::conclusion",
        "PMC6197204::web::019::microhardness_and_magnetic_properties"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Strengthened domain-wall pinning will increase coercivity relative to the same alloy in its as-cast or solution-treated state.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11426066::web::019::conclusion",
        "PMC6197204::web::019::microhardness_and_magnetic_properties"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The treatment will increase coercivity by roughly three- to four-fold.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The solution-treated FeCoNi-based baseline has coercivity below 10 Oe or on the order of a few Oe.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6197204::web::019::microhardness_and_magnetic_properties"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The coercivity increase will occur without significantly reducing saturation magnetization.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The treated material will preserve the strong magnetization characteristic of FeCoNi-based alloys.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11426066::web::019::conclusion",
        "PMC6197204::web::019::microhardness_and_magnetic_properties"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The treated material will preserve high-entropy single-phase character despite forming precipitates.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Annealing above 600 °C or for excessively long times risks microstructural coarsening.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Higher-temperature or excessive annealing will diminish the coercivity enhancement.",
